WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.924
Semantic HTML describes the meaning of content, not only its visual appearance.

00:00:04.924 --> 00:00:11.080
Headings, navigation, main content, articles and buttons give browsers and assistive technologies a useful structure.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:17.235
A large bold paragraph does not become a heading merely because it looks like one.

00:00:18.235 --> 00:00:21.610
Use an anchor with a meaningful href for navigation.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.610
It supplies familiar link semantics and keyboard behaviour.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:29.110
A button is appropriate when the control performs an in-page action instead.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.852
Which element normally performs an in-page action?

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:36.770
A button is the appropriate interactive control for an action.
